  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 1.0.7\n\n### Security\n- Upgraded RestSharp from 106.11.7 to 114.0.0 to fix known vulnerabilities:\n  - GHSA-9pq7-rcxv-47vq (high): incorrect regular expression (RestSharp <= 106.11.7)\n  - GHSA-4rr6-2v9v-wcpc (moderate): CRLF injection in `RestRequest.AddHeader` (RestSharp 107.0.0 - 111.x)\n- Removed the vulnerable transitive dependency System.Text.Encodings.Web 5.0.0 (GHSA-ghhp-997w-qr28, critical).\n\n### Compatibility notes\n- The public API of NopaperSDK is unchanged: no code changes are needed to call `NopaperClient`.\n- If your project uses RestSharp directly, it will now resolve to RestSharp 114. Code written for the old RestSharp API (`IRestResponse`, `new RestRequest(Method.POST)`, `client.Authenticator = ...`) must be updated to the RestSharp 107+ API. If your project pins an older RestSharp version, the restore fails with NU1605.\n- On .NET Framework and .NET Standard 2.0, RestSharp 114 adds a dependency on System.Text.Json 10.0.0 or later. On .NET Framework you may need binding redirects.\n- .NET Framework 4.7.1 or later is required.",
